modesetting: link against libgbm

The modesetting driver calls gbm_bo_* directly whenever it is built with
GLAMOR_HAS_GBM, but its autotools link line only lists UDEV_LIBS and DRM_LIBS.
GBM_LIBS is computed by configure and then never used, so modesetting_drv.so
ships with twelve unresolved gbm_* symbols and the X server refuses to load it:

    (EE) Failed to load .../modesetting_drv.so: undefined symbol:
         gbm_bo_get_plane_count
    (EE) No drivers available.
    Fatal server error: no screens found

Distributions do not hit this because something else in their server pulls
libgbm into the global symbol namespace first. On a minimal Buildroot rootfs
nothing does, so the driver has to link it itself.

Patches Makefile.in rather than Makefile.am so that no autoreconf is needed;
the patch leaves Makefile.in newer than Makefile.am, so automake's rebuild
rules stay quiet.

Signed-off-by: Chronopolis firmware build

diff --git a/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/Makefile.in b/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/Makefile.in
--- a/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/Makefile.in
+++ b/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/Makefile.in
@@ -636,7 +636,7 @@

 modesetting_drv_la_LTLIBRARIES = modesetting_drv.la
 modesetting_drv_la_LDFLAGS = -module -avoid-version
-modesetting_drv_la_LIBADD = $(UDEV_LIBS) $(DRM_LIBS)
+modesetting_drv_la_LIBADD = $(UDEV_LIBS) $(DRM_LIBS) $(GBM_LIBS)
 modesetting_drv_ladir = @moduledir@/drivers
 modesetting_drv_la_SOURCES = \
 	 dri2.c \
